role: The Officer, Deakin HELP is instrumental in resolving frontline enquiries across people, finance, systems and general work requests, and supporting a broad range of University stakeholders to enable timely, accurate resolution of Tier 1 service needs. Operating with increasing independence, the role collaborates within the Customer Support team and escalates complex matters to Tier 2 support as needed. The position contributes to continuous improvement of the knowledge bank and supports effective, consistent service delivery across all channels. As an Officer, Deakin HELP, you will: Handle a broad range of frontline enquiries relating to people, finance, work requests, providing accurate advice across phone, email, ticketing and face-to-face channels Collect and analyse information from a range of sources to identify practical solutions, presenting information clearly to support timely resolution and decision-making Build and maintain productive relationships with a diverse range of stakeholders, tailoring communication style to meet audience needs Identify and escalate complex or unresolved enquiries to Tier 2 support as needed, applying sound judgement to determine when escalation is required Deliver effective and efficient outcomes against team and operational work plans, meeting agreed service standards and timelines To be successful, you’ll have: Degree without subsequent experience; or Diploma with experience; or Post Trades Certificate/Advanced Certificate with relevant experience; or equivalent combination of experience and/or education/training Experience providing advice or support services Strong communication and stakeholder engagement skills Ability to interpret and apply procedures Experience coordinating work and managing priorities Here's how to apply: Please submit your updated resume and a short cover letter outlining your skills and experience. For a confidential discussion regarding this role, please contact Bandish Kachhy (Assistant Manager, Deakin HELP) via email bandish.kachhy@deakin.edu.au For a copy of the position description, please see below: PD - Officer, Deakin HELP - HEW 5.pdf Applications for this position close at 11.55pm on 27 September 2026. Are You Ready? Deakin is a Victorian university with a global impact. We are an agile, dynamic, and innovative university committed to making a positive impact through our excellence in education, research and innovation and the contributions we make to the wider community. We understand that our reputation has been built on the dedication and expertise of our staff and we offer a dynamic and diverse working environment with opportunities to grow and develop careers. We believe that a progressive, thriving culture will ensure that people choose to come, and stay at Deakin and contribute to our ongoing success. We value diversity and aim to build an inclusive environment that champions, embraces and respects differences. We support and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and people of all abilities, cultures, sexual orientation, and genders. Pre-employment safety and suitability checks: In accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence, appointment to this role is subject to successful completion of relevant pre-employment checks, including Working With Children Checks and candidate gender-based violence declarations. Candidates may be asked to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender‑based Violence, or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender‑based Violence during the course of their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process.  A declaration is not required from individuals who have experienced gender‑based violence.  A ‘Yes’ response does not automatically exclude a candidate from employment, and any information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for relevance to the role and the University’s safety obligations. Advertised: 11 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 27 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Officer, Deakin HELP Flexible, Geelong - City, Melbourne - Burwood 27 Sep 2026 Be the first point of contact for Deakin staff, resolving frontline enquiries across people, finance, systems and general work requests. You’ll connect with a diverse range of University stakeholders to deliver timely, accurate and exceptional Tier 1 service. Current opportunities Position Location Closes Officer, Deakin HELP Flexible, Geelong - City, Melbourne - Burwood 27 Sep 2026 Be the first point of contact for Deakin staff, resolving frontline enquiries across people, finance, systems and general work requests. You’ll connect with a diverse range of University stakeholders to deliver timely, accurate and exceptional Tier 1 service. Powered by PageUp Copyright Disclaimer Privacy Sitemap Jobs at Deakin Deakin Integrity Donate Emergency information Contact us Accessibility Connect with Deakin Facebook Twitter Instagram Linkedin This WeChat YouTube Atar calculator Atar calculator We acknowledge the traditional owners of the lands on which Deakin University stands and we pay our respect. © Copyright Deakin University 2026. Deakin University CRICOS Provider Code: 00113B."
