orks across Deakin to support innovation, entrepreneurship and commercialisation. Partnering with faculties, researchers, students and industry, the team creates opportunities that transform ideas into meaningful impact To be successful, you’ll have: Experience in entrepreneurship, innovation or startup environments, with an understanding of venture development activities. Demonstrated ability to build collaborative partnerships and influence a broad range of stakeholders. Experience leading programs, projects or initiatives and delivering outcomes aligned to strategic objectives. Strong communication, storytelling, audience engagement and visual design skills, with the ability to translate complex concepts into accessible content. Demonstrated ability to drive innovation, continuous improvement and effective outcomes in complex environments Here's how to apply: Please submit your updated resume and a short cover letter outlining your skills and experience. Want to Know More? For a confidential discussion regarding this role, please contact Glynn Atkinson (Senior Director, Business Development & Commercialisation) on glynn.atkinson@deakin.edu.au For a copy of the position description, please see below: PD - Specialist, Engagement.pdf Applications for this position close on 24 th September at 11:55pm Are You Ready? Deakin is a Victorian university with a global impact. We are an agile, dynamic, and innovative university committed to making a positive impact through our excellence in education, research and innovation and the contributions we make to the wider community. We understand that our reputation has been built on the dedication and expertise of our staff and we offer a dynamic and diverse working environment with opportunities to grow and develop careers. We believe that a progressive, thriving culture will ensure that people choose to come, and stay at Deakin and contribute to our ongoing success. We value diversity and aim to build an inclusive environment 