thways Visas Students under 18 Previous study - academic requirements Fees and scholarships Why study in Australia? Living in Australia Before you arrive Information for parents and families How to apply Study abroad and exchange Study abroad Exchange Specialised programs Academic information Get help or contact Deakin Support in your country or region Research Research Research strengths Improving health and wellbeing Designing smarter technologies Enabling a sustainable world Advancing society and culture Building safe and secure communities Research partnerships Research for industry and government Strategic research partnerships Deakin Energy Future Food ManuFutures Research groups Institutes and centres Faculties and schools Collaborative research groups Find a researcher Research degrees and PhD Find a research degree How to find a research supervisor Research applications Research degree entry pathways Fees, funding and scholarships Key dates for research students International research students Support for researchers Project funding Manage a project Establish a project Research data management Research integrity Research news and publications Publications Our research response to COVID-19 Business and community Business and community University partnerships International partnerships Research partnerships Employ students and graduates Short courses Community engagement Melbourne Burwood Geelong Warrnambool Riverina Murray Bendigo Western Metropolitan Melbourne Event services Donate How to donate Areas to support About Deakin About Deakin Locations Campuses Deakin learning centres Corporate centres International offices Faculties and divisions Arts and Education Business and Law Health Science, Engineering and Built Environment Research Administrative divisions Leadership and governance Vice-Chancellor University Executive Organisational structure and management Legislation and policy library Reputation and recognition History Awards World-class research Vision and values Deakin's strategic direction Teaching and learning Culture Diversity and inclusion Sustainability Work at Deakin Job vacancies How to apply Why work at Deakin? Teaching at Deakin Living in Australia News and media releases Help hub Change Language Language English English Language Russian Pусский Language Chinese 中国 Language Korean 한국어 Language Chinese 中國 Language Spanish Español Language Vietnamese tiếng Việt Language Portugese Português Language Malaysian Bahasa Malaysia Language Thai ภาษาไทย Language Indonesian Bahasa Indonesia Language Arabic العربية Library Staff Current students Contact Deakin My courses 0 Home About Deakin Work at Deakin Careers Existing Applicant Login Job alert Work type Full-time 1 Part-time 1 Locations Australia Melbourne - Burwood 1 Categories Academic Health 1 Senior Teaching Fellow (Clinical Educator) Apply now Job no: 589015 Work type: Full-time, Part-time Location: Melbourne - Burwood Categories: Health Based at our Melbourne Burwood Campus + hybrid work arrangements Full-time or part-time and fixed term until 30 June 2027 Level C $149,230 - $171,602 (pro rata part-time) + 17% Superannuation Why this role matters: Join the Deakin University School of Psychology as a Senior Teaching Fellow (Clinical Educator) and play a pivotal role in shaping the future of psychology education and clinical training. This is a unique opportunity to establish and lead a psychology training clinic, creating real-world learning experiences that prepare postgraduate students to become confident, capable and impactful practitioners. In this influential role, you'll combine clinical leadership, teaching excellence and strategic partnership development to strengthen student learning, expand placement opportunities and enhance community engagement. From supervising future psychologists and driving curriculum innovation, to building meaningful collaborations with health and community organisations, you'll help deliver outstanding outcomes for students, the profession and the broader community We're looking for an experienced and passionate clinical educator who thrives on mentoring others, fostering high-quality learning environments and turning new ideas into reality. If you're excited by the opportunity to shape a flagship training initiative, lead innovation in psychology education and leave a lasting legacy for future generations of psychologists, we'd love to hear from you. As a Senior Teaching Fellow (Clinical Educator) you will: Lead the establishment, operation and continuous improvement of a psychology training clinic, ensuring high-quality clinical education and service delivery. Provide clinical supervision and mentoring to postgraduate psychology placement students, supporting their professional development and readiness for practice. Build and strengthen partnerships with health, community and industry organisations to expand placement opportunities and enhance teaching, learning and research outcomes. Drive excellence in teaching and learning through curriculum innovation, quality improvement initiatives and evidence-informed educational practices. Contribute to governance, accreditation and clinical quality processes while fostering a collaborative and inclusive learning environment for students and colleagues. To be successful, you’ll have: General registration as a psychologist with the Psychology Board of Australia, Board-approved supervisor status, and clinical endorsement. Extensive post-registration clinical experience, including psychological assessment and therapy across adult and child/adolescent populations. Demonstrated experience supervising provisional psychologists or placement students in clinical settings. Proven ability to establish, manage or lead clinical services, including governance, quality and risk management. A strong track record in teaching, curriculum development and building partnerships that enhance student and community outcomes. Here's how to apply: Please submit your updated resume, a short cover letter and responses to the Key Selection Criteria. For a confidential discussion regarding this role, please contact Elizabeth Westrupp (Associate Head of School, Research) on elizabeth.westrupp@deakin.edu.au. For a copy of the position description, please see below: PD - Senior Teaching Fellow, 589015.pdf Applications for this position close on Thursday 15th October at 11:55pm. Benefits for working with us! At Deakin, we offer more than just a job. We offer a rewarding career in a flexible, inclusive and forward-thinking environment. Across our campuses in Geelong, Melbourne and regional Victoria, you'll enjoy flexible working arrangements that support work-life balance, generous leave provisions including extended parental leave and the option to purchase additional leave, and access to a range of professional development opportunities to help you grow your career. Are You Ready? Deakin is a Victorian university with a global impact. We are an agile, dynamic, and innovative university committed to making a positive impact through our excellence in education, research and innovation and the contributions we make to the wider community. We understand that our reputation has been built on the dedication and expertise of our staff and we offer a dynamic and diverse working environment with opportunities to grow and develop careers. We believe that a progressive, thriving culture will ensure that people choose to come, and stay at Deakin and contribute to our ongoing success. We value diversity and aim to build an inclusive environment that champions, embraces and respects differences. We support and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and people of all abilities, cultures, sexual orientation, and genders. Pre-employment safety and suitability checks: In accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence, appointment to this role is subject to successful completion of relevant pre-employment checks, including Working With Children Checks and candidate gender-based violence declarations. Candidates may be asked to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender‑based Violence, or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender‑based Violence during the course of their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process.  A declaration is not required from individuals who have experienced gender‑based violence.  A ‘Yes’ response does not automatically exclude a candidate from employment, and any information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for relevance to the role and the University’s safety obligations. Advertised: 17 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Senior Teaching Fellow (Clinical Educator) Melbourne - Burwood 15 Oct 2026 Join us in shaping the future of psychology education and clinical training. You’ll lead the establishment and operation of an innovative psychology training clinic, supervise postgraduate placement students, and foster impactful partnerships with industry and community stakeholders. This is a unique opportunity to drive excellence in teaching, enhance student learning experiences, influence clinical placement outcomes, and contribute to the ongoing growth and reputation of Deakin University's psychology programs. Current opportunities Position Location Closes Senior Teaching Fellow (Clinical Educator) Melbourne - Burwood 15 Oct 2026 Join us in shaping the future of psychology education and clinical training. You’ll lead the establishment and operation of an innovative psychology training clinic, supervise postgraduate placement students, and foster impactful partnerships with industry and community stakeholders. This is a unique opportunity to drive excellence in teaching, enhance student learning experiences, influence clinical placement outcomes, and contribute to the ongoing growth and reputation of Deakin University's psychology programs. Powered by PageUp Copyright Disclaimer Privacy Sitemap Jobs at Deakin Deakin Integrity Donate Emergency information Contact us Accessibility Connect with Deakin Facebook Twitter Instagram Linkedin This WeChat YouTube Atar calculator Atar calculator We acknowledge the traditional owners of the lands on which Deakin University stands and we pay our respect. © Copyright Deakin University . Deakin University CRICOS Provider Code: 00113B."
