ion and values Deakin's strategic direction Teaching and learning Culture Diversity and inclusion Sustainability Work at Deakin Job vacancies How to apply Why work at Deakin? Teaching at Deakin Living in Australia News and media releases Help hub Change Language Language English English Language Russian Pусский Language Chinese 中国 Language Korean 한국어 Language Chinese 中國 Language Spanish Español Language Vietnamese tiếng Việt Language Portugese Português Language Malaysian Bahasa Malaysia Language Thai ภาษาไทย Language Indonesian Bahasa Indonesia Language Arabic العربية Library Staff Current students Contact Deakin My courses 0 Home About Deakin Work at Deakin Careers Existing Applicant Login Job alert Work type Full-time 1 Locations Australia Melbourne - Burwood 1 Categories Professional Building and Property Services 1 Senior Officer, Campus Maintenance Apply now Job no: 589338 Work type: Full-time Location: Melbourne - Burwood Categories: Building and Property Services ​​Based at our Melbourne, Burwood Campus​ + hybrid work arrangements Full-time & Continuing $100,128 - $108,130 (HEW 6) + 17% Superannuation Ready for your next opportunity? We're seeking an experienced facilities management professional to oversee maintenance activities across our Deakin campuses. A trade qualification and hands-on technical background will be highly regarded, offering the opportunity to apply your technical expertise and knowledge in a dynamic and rewarding university environment. In this role, you'll help shape the day-to-day experience of thousands of students and staff by ensuring Deakin's campuses are safe, functional and well maintained. Working alongside contractors, stakeholders and the Property Services team, you'll coordinate maintenance activities, deliver practical solutions and contribute to continuous improvements across our campus facilities, infrastructure and services. The role at a glance: Coordinate and oversee routine maintenance activities across campus facilities Manage maintenance requests, prioritising work and ensuring timely resolution Liaise with contractors and service providers to deliver maintenance works safely, efficiently, and to a high standard Conduct facility inspections and identify maintenance requirements Support preventative maintenance programs that improve reliability and asset performance Monitor contractor performance and maintain accurate maintenance records Work collaboratively with a broad range of stakeholders to minimise disruption and deliver excellent service outcomes Contribute to creating safe, efficient, and well-maintained campus environments To be successful, you’ll have: Experience in facilities management, maintenance coordination, building services, or asset maintenance Trade qualifications and hands-on maintenance experience will be highly regarded Demonstrated knowledge of building systems and maintenance practices, including areas such as HVAC, electrical, plumbing, mechanical services and general building maintenance Excellent stakeholder and contractor management skills Strong organisational skills and the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously A proactive, customer-focused approach to problem solving Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively within a team Who are we? Deakin is a cutting-edge public university headquartered in Victoria, revolutionising education with 61,000 students across our campuses: Melbourne Burwood, Geelong Waurn Ponds, Geelong Waterfront, Warrnambool, Deakin University Lancaster University Indonesia (DLI), GIFT City, India, and our vibrant online environment. We're proud to be a progressive and open-minded university, delivering the highest student satisfaction in Victoria and consistently ranked in the top 1% of the world's universities. Why work with us? At Deakin you will have access to benefits such as a variety of leave options including generous parental leave and the ability to purchase additional leave; flexible working arrangements to help manage your work-life balance; ongoing learning and development opportunities to grow your career; an inclusive and supportive culture and environment to work in, both online and on campus. Here's how to apply: Please submit your updated resume and a short cover letter outlining your skills and experience. For a confidential discussion regarding this role, please contact Jason Grima (Senior Coordinator, Campus Maintenance) on jason.grima@deakin.edu.au For a copy of the position description, please see below: PD - Senior Officer Campus Maintenance.pdf Applications for this position close on Monday 5 October 2026 at 11.55PM. Are You Ready? Deakin is a Victorian university with a global impact. We are an agile, dynamic, and innovative university committed to making a positive impact through our excellence in education, research and innovation and the contributions we make to the wider community. We understand that our reputation has been built on the dedication and expertise of our staff and we offer a dynamic and diverse working environment with opportunities to grow and develop careers. We believe that a progressive, thriving culture will ensure that people choose to come, and stay at Deakin and contribute to our ongoing success. We value diversity and aim to build an inclusive environment that champions, embraces and respects differences. We support and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and people of all abilities, cultures, sexual orientation, and genders. Pre-employment safety and suitability checks: In accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence, appointment to this role is subject to successful completion of relevant pre-employment checks, including Working With Children Checks and candidate gender-based violence declarations. Candidates may be asked to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender‑based Violence, or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender‑based Violence during the course of their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. A declaration is not required from individuals who have experienced gender‑based violence. A ‘Yes’ response does not automatically exclude a candidate from employment, and any information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for relevance to the role and the University’s safety obligations. Advertised: 21 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 05 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Senior Officer, Campus Maintenance Melbourne - Burwood 5 Oct 2026 Play a key role in maintaining Deakin's Burwood campuses, coordinating maintenance activities and delivering safe, high-quality facilities for students and staff. Current opportunities Position Location Closes Senior Officer, Campus Maintenance Melbourne - Burwood 5 Oct 2026 Play a key role in maintaining Deakin's Burwood campuses, coordinating maintenance activities and delivering safe, high-quality facilities for students and staff. Powered by PageUp Copyright Disclaimer Privacy Sitemap Jobs at Deakin Deakin Integrity Donate Emergency information Contact us Accessibility Connect with Deakin Facebook Twitter Instagram Linkedin This WeChat YouTube Atar calculator Atar calculator We acknowledge the traditional owners of the lands on which Deakin University stands and we pay our respect. © Copyright Deakin University 2026. Deakin University CRICOS Provider Code: 00113B."
